  "description": "Automatic-channel seed: seed = splitmix64(fnv1a64(bytes)), bytes = ASCII server ID (32 lower-case hex) || 0x00 || ASCII kind (library, genre, collection or recipe) || 0x00 || key. The key is the 32 ASCII hex characters of the canonical ID for a library or a collection, the exact UTF-8 bytes of the name for a genre, and the recipe key (1 to 64 characters of a-z, 0-9 and hyphen) for a recipe, with no case folding and no Unicode normalisation (the last two genre rows are the same word in another case and in another normalisation form: different seeds). Every 64-bit value is an object: dec (unsigned decimal string), hex (16 lower-case digits, no prefix), hi and lo (its high and low 32 bits as 8 lower-case hex digits), so a port without a native 64-bit integer can check each step. Placeholder IDs only. Whitespace, control and format characters are written as JSON escapes (such as \\u00a0 for a no-break space) so that they can be seen.",
